{"id":"9207f2b8918f7468c645ce27456c843a75eb4119","axis":"silent","repo":"quarkusio/quarkus","sha":"9207f2b8918f7468c645ce27456c843a75eb4119","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/security-oidc-code-flow-authentication.adoc","lines":["@@ -1711,12 +1711,21 @@ quarkus.oidc.application-type=web-app"," quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.path=/back-channel-logout"," ----"," ","-The absolute `back-channel logout` URL is calculated by adding `quarkus.oidc.back-channel-logout.path` to the current endpoint URL, for example, `http://localhost:8080/back-channel-logout`.","+The absolute `back-channel logout` URL is calculated by adding `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.path` to the current endpoint URL, for example, `http://localhost:8080/back-channel-logout`."," You will need to configure this URL in the admin console of your OIDC provider."," "," You will also need to configure a token age property for the logout token verification to succeed if your OIDC provider does not set an expiry claim in the current logout token."," For example, set `quarkus.oidc.token.age=10S` to ensure that no more than 10 seconds elapse since the logout token's `iat` (issued at) time."," ","+A logout token which has a `sid` (session id) claim logs out only the session whose ID token has the same `sid` claim, so make sure that the OIDC provider includes the `sid` claim in its ID tokens.","+By default, a logout token without the `sid` claim logs out only one session of the user identified by the logout token `sub` (subject) claim: the first session which accesses the application after the logout token has arrived.","+If the same user logs in from several browsers, set `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.logout-all-sessions=true` to log out every session this user had when the logout token was issued.","+Quarkus then keeps such a logout token cached and makes a best effort to log out all the other sessions of this user.","+A logout token stays cached until the session it targets accesses the application, which may never happen.","+A logout token which targets all the sessions of the user is removed only by the cleanup timer or when the cache is full.","+Set `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.clean-up-timer-interval` to activate the cleanup timer and keep `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.token-cache-time-to-live` short so that stale logout tokens are removed promptly.","+Increase `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.token-cache-size` if many logout tokens can arrive within this period.","+"," [[front-channel-logout]]"," ==== Front-channel logout"," "],"additions":10,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/security-oidc-expanded-configuration.adoc","lines":["@@ -759,6 +759,7 @@ PLease be aware that supporting the back-channel logout option requires managing"," "," |quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.path || Back-channel logout path"," |quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.logout-token-key |`sub` claim| Back-channel logout token key","+|quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.logout-all-sessions |false| Log out all user sessions"," |quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.token-cache-size |10| Back-channel logout token cache size"," |quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.token-cache-time-to-live |10 minutes| Back-channel logout token cache time to live"," |quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.clean-up-timer-interval || Back-channel logout token cache clean up interval","@@ -768,6 +769,9 @@ PLease be aware that supporting the back-channel logout option requires managing"," "," The back-channel notification contains a logout token. It must be cached so that when one of the authenticated users tries to access Quarkus, this user's ID token can be matched against this logout token. The subject (`sub`) claim value is used by default to match the ID and logout tokens, but the session id (`sid`) claim can be used instead."," ","+Set `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.logout-all-sessions=true` to log out all the sessions that the user had when a logout token without the `sid` claim was issued, for example, when the user has logged in from several browsers.","+This property cannot be enabled when `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.logout-token-key` is set to `sid`.","+"," `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.token-cache-size`, `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.token-cache-time-to-live` and `quarkus.oidc.logout.backchannel.clean-up-timer-interval` are properties for managing the back-channel notification cache."," "," [NOTE]"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/BackChannelLogoutHandler.java","lines":["@@ -173,17 +173,14 @@ public void accept(MultiMap form) {","                                                 .verifyLogoutJwtToken(encodedLogoutToken);"," ","                                         if (verifyLogoutTokenClaims(result)) {","-                                            String key = result.localVerificationResult()","-                                                    .getString(","-                                                            tenantContext.oidcConfig().logout().backchannel().logoutTokenKey());","                                             BackChannelLogoutTokenCache tokens = resolver.getBackChannelLogoutTokens()","                                                     .get(tenantId);","                                             if (tokens == null) {","-                                                tokens = new BackChannelLogoutTokenCache(tenantContext.oidcConfig(),","-                                                        context.vertx());","-                                                resolver.getBackChannelLogoutTokens().put(tenantId, tokens);","+                                                tokens = resolver.getBackChannelLogoutTokens().computeIfAbsent(tenantId,","+                                                        k -> new BackChannelLogoutTokenCache(tenantContext.oidcConfig(),","+                                                                context.vertx()));","                                             }","-                                            tokens.addTokenVerification(key, result);","+                                            tokens.addTokenVerification(result);"," ","                                             if (resolver.isSecurityEventObserved()) {","                                                 SecurityEventHelper.fire(resolver.getSecurityEvent(),","@@ -230,6 +227,12 @@ private boolean verifyLogoutTokenClaims(TokenVerificationResult result) {","                 LOG.debug(\"Back channel logout token must not contain 'nonce' claim\");","                 return false;","             }","+            if (tenantContext.oidcConfig().logout().backchannel().logoutAllSessions()","+                    && !result.localVerificationResult().containsKey(OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM)","+                    && !result.localVerificationResult().containsKey(Claims.iat.name())) {","+                LOG.debug(\"Back channel logout token without 'sid' claim must contain 'iat' claim to log out all the sessions\");","+                return false;","+            }"," ","             return true;","         }"],"additions":10,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/BackChannelLogoutTokenCache.java","lines":["@@ -1,30 +1,138 @@"," package io.quarkus.oidc.runtime;"," ","+import org.eclipse.microprofile.jwt.Claims;","+import org.jboss.logging.Logger;","+","+import io.quarkus.oidc.common.runtime.OidcConstants;"," import io.vertx.core.Vertx;","+import io.vertx.core.json.JsonObject;"," "," public class BackChannelLogoutTokenCache {"," ","-    final MemoryCache<TokenVerificationResult> cache;","+    private static final Logger LOG = Logger.getLogger(BackChannelLogoutTokenCache.class);","+    private static final String CACHE_KEY_SEPARATOR = \"|\";","+","+    private final MemoryCache<TokenVerificationResult> cache;","+    private final String logoutTokenKey;","+    private final boolean logoutTokenKeyIsSid;","+    private final boolean logoutAllSessions;"," ","     public BackChannelLogoutTokenCache(OidcTenantConfig oidcTenantConfig, Vertx vertx) {","-        cache = new MemoryCache<TokenVerificationResult>(vertx, oidcTenantConfig.logout().backchannel().cleanUpTimerInterval(),","-                oidcTenantConfig.logout().backchannel().tokenCacheTimeToLive(),","-                oidcTenantConfig.logout().backchannel().tokenCacheSize());","+        OidcTenantConfig.Backchannel backchannel = oidcTenantConfig.logout().backchannel();","+        cache = new MemoryCache<>(vertx, backchannel.cleanUpTimerInterval(),","+                backchannel.tokenCacheTimeToLive(), backchannel.tokenCacheSize());","+        logoutTokenKey = backchannel.logoutTokenKey();","+        logoutTokenKeyIsSid = OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM.equals(logoutTokenKey);","+        logoutAllSessions = backchannel.logoutAllSessions();","     }"," ","-    public void addTokenVerification(String token, TokenVerificationResult result) {","-        cache.add(token, result);","+    public void addTokenVerification(TokenVerificationResult logoutToken) {","+        JsonObject claims = logoutToken.localVerificationResult();","+        if (logoutAllSessions && claims.getString(OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM) == null) {","+            removeRedundantSessionLogoutTokens(claims);","+        }","+        cache.add(cacheKey(claims), logoutToken);","     }"," ","-    public TokenVerificationResult removeTokenVerification(String token) {","-        return cache.remove(token);","+    public TokenVerificationResult findLogoutToken(JsonObject idTokenJson) {","+        String logoutTokenKeyValue = idTokenJson.getString(logoutTokenKey);","+        if (logoutTokenKeyValue == null) {","+            return null;","+        }","+        TokenVerificationResult logoutToken = null;","+        if (!logoutTokenKeyIsSid) {","+            String idTokenSid = idTokenJson.getString(OidcConstants.ID_TOKEN_SID_CLAIM);","+            if (idTokenSid != null) {","+                // logout token with the session id targets only the session identified by it","+                logoutToken = findLogoutToken(sessionCacheKey(logoutTokenKeyValue, idTokenSid), idTokenJson);","+            }","+        }","+        if (logoutToken == null) {","+            // logout token without the session id matches any session of the subject created before the token was issued,","+            // logoutCompleted decides whether it is dropped after the first logout or kept to log out all the sessions","+            logoutToken = findLogoutToken(logoutTokenKeyValue, idTokenJson);","+        }","+        return logoutToken;","     }"," ","-    public boolean containsTokenVerification(String token) {","-        return cache.containsKey(token);","+    public void logoutCompleted(TokenVerificationResult logoutToken) {","+        JsonObject claims = logoutToken.localVerificationResult();","+        if (logoutAllSessions && claims.getString(OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM) == null) {","+            // keep the logout token cached so that the other sessions of the subject are logged out too","+            return;","+        }","+        cache.remove(cacheKey(claims));","     }"," ","     void shutdown(Vertx vertx) {","         cache.stopTimer(vertx);","     }","+","+    private TokenVerificationResult findLogoutToken(String cacheKey, JsonObject idTokenJson) {","+        TokenVerificationResult logoutToken = cache.get(cacheKey);","+        if (logoutToken != null && targetsSession(logoutToken.localVerificationResult(), idTokenJson)) {","+            return logoutToken;","+        }","+        return null;","+    }","+","+    private void removeRedundantSessionLogoutTokens(JsonObject subjectLogoutTokenJson) {","+        String logoutTokenKeyValue = subjectLogoutTokenJson.getString(logoutTokenKey);","+        Long subjectLogoutTokenIssuedAt = subjectLogoutTokenJson.getLong(Claims.iat.name());","+        cache.removeIf(cachedLogoutToken -> {","+            JsonObject cachedLogoutTokenJson = cachedLogoutToken.localVerificationResult();","+            return cachedLogoutTokenJson.getString(OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM) != null","+                    && logoutTokenKeyValue.equals(cachedLogoutTokenJson.getString(logoutTokenKey))","+                    && !isIssuedAfter(cachedLogoutTokenJson, subjectLogoutTokenIssuedAt);","+        });","+    }","+","+    private String cacheKey(JsonObject logoutTokenJson) {","+        String logoutTokenKeyValue = logoutTokenJson.getString(logoutTokenKey);","+        if (logoutTokenKeyIsSid) {","+            return logoutTokenKeyValue;","+        }","+        String logoutTokenSid = logoutTokenJson.getString(OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM);","+        return logoutTokenSid == null ? logoutTokenKeyValue : sessionCacheKey(logoutTokenKeyValue, logoutTokenSid);","+    }","+","+    private static String sessionCacheKey(String logoutTokenKeyValue, String sid) {","+        // the key is only an index, a collision is harmless because targetsSession","+        // compares the subject and the session id claims separately","+        return logoutTokenKeyValue + CACHE_KEY_SEPARATOR + sid;","+    }","+","+    private static boolean targetsSession(JsonObject logoutTokenJson, JsonObject idTokenJson) {","+        String logoutTokenIss = logoutTokenJson.getString(Claims.iss.name());","+        if (logoutTokenIss != null && !logoutTokenIss.equals(idTokenJson.getString(Claims.iss.name()))) {","+            LOG.debug(\"Logout token issuer does not match the ID token issuer\");","+            return false;","+        }","+        String logoutTokenSub = logoutTokenJson.getString(Claims.sub.name());","+        String idTokenSub = idTokenJson.getString(Claims.sub.name());","+        if (logoutTokenSub != null && idTokenSub != null && !logoutTokenSub.equals(idTokenSub)) {","+            LOG.debug(\"Logout token subject does not match the ID token subject\");","+            return false;","+        }","+        String logoutTokenSid = logoutTokenJson.getString(OidcConstants.BACK_CHANNEL_LOGOUT_SID_CLAIM);","+        String idTokenSid = idTokenJson.getString(OidcConstants.ID_TOKEN_SID_CLAIM);","+        if (logoutTokenSid != null && idTokenSid != null && !logoutTokenSid.equals(idTokenSid)) {","+            LOG.debug(\"Logout token session id does not match the ID token session id\");","+            return false;","+        }","+        if (logoutTokenSid == null && isIdTokenIssuedAfterLogoutToken(idTokenJson, logoutTokenJson)) {","+            LOG.trace(\"ID token was issued after the logout token, the session is not affected\");","+            return false;","+        }","+        return true;","+    }","+","+    private static boolean isIdTokenIssuedAfterLogoutToken(JsonObject idToken, JsonObject logoutToken) {","+        return isIssuedAfter(idToken, logoutToken.getLong(Claims.iat.name()));","+    }","+","+    private static boolean isIssuedAfter(JsonObject token, Long issuedAt) {","+        Long tokenIssuedAt = token.getLong(Claims.iat.name());","+        return tokenIssuedAt != null && issuedAt != null && tokenIssuedAt > issuedAt;","+    }"," }"],"additions":118,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/CodeAuthenticationMechanism.java","lines":["@@ -554,66 +554,37 @@ private boolean isLogout(RoutingContext context, TenantConfigContext configConte","     }"," ","     private boolean isBackChannelLogoutPending(TenantConfigContext configContext, SecurityIdentity identity) {","-        if (configContext.oidcConfig().logout().backchannel().path().isEmpty()) {","-            return false;","-        }","-        BackChannelLogoutTokenCache tokens = resolver.getBackChannelLogoutTokens()","-                .get(configContext.oidcConfig().ten